diff --git a/research/JSRF_V9_ABI_ROOT_CAUSE.md b/research/JSRF_V9_ABI_ROOT_CAUSE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e058952
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/JSRF_V9_ABI_ROOT_CAUSE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# JSRF v9 ABI root-cause note
+
+The v9 Windows run reached the same `sub_001579D0` crash, but `RECOMP_ABI_CHECK`
+made the earlier stack damage visible.
+
+## First actionable violation
+
+`sub_00154E00` returned with `ESP 0x00F7FE8C -> 0x00F7FE88`.  The retail body
+pushes `ESI`/`EDI`, invokes the vtable method at slot `+0x1C`, then returns with
+`ret 4`.  On the failing branch that first virtual method is the only callee.
+The missing 12 bytes are therefore exactly the virtual method's retail
+`ret 0x0C` argument cleanup.
+
+The object is a JSRF interface whose vtable begins at `0x001E0F00`; slot `+0x1C`
+is the retail function `0x00154D70`.  That function is vtable-only, has no
+standard frame prologue, starts cleanly after the preceding `ret`/padding, and
+all of its retail exits use `ret 0x0C`.
+
+## Same detector shape elsewhere
+
+Two later ABI failures have the same vtable-only/non-prologue shape:
+
+- `0x00155380`, stored at `0x001E0F18`.
+- `0x0015A020`, stored at `0x001E13FC`.
+
+Both are clear standalone retail functions separated from their predecessors by
+`ret` plus padding, yet neither has a standard `push ebp; mov ebp, esp`
+prologue.  The generic data-pointer recovery can materialize this shape as an
+alias after function boundaries are already fixed.  v9 shows those alias-built
+entries returning with corrupted callee-saved state/ESP.
+
+## Bring-up fix
+
+Seed those three proven retail entries before function construction:
+
+- `0x00154D70`
+- `0x00155380`
+- `0x0015A020`
+
+This is not a gameplay or behavior override.  It changes only the static
+function-boundary input so xboxrecomp lifts the original retail bodies with
+their own epilogues/`ret N` cleanup.
+
+The tester also captures the generated C source context named by DbgHelp on a
+future crash, so the next run will preserve the exact lifted statements without
+manual file hunting.
